David Damerell wrote:

> Quoting  Matthew Ward  <nsquarticsurface@gmail.com>:
>>I'm playing a wizard and got a pretty good start. Now I'm pretty sure I'll 
>>die, because I got one of those Big Rooms that contain the stairs to Sokoba
>>n. It feels too early to survive. What do people do in this situation?
>
> Try and arrange to be Fast, then have a copy of the Benny Hill music to
> hand. Once you're Fast, you can kite the monsters around the bigroom with
> almost complete impunity.
>
> Obviously, stick your nose in first to see what's what... but bear in mind
> that the Sokoban stairs just provide another exit for when things get too
> hot.

I was working on an AI for TAEB (a NetHack-playing bot) a while ago,
which I tried to code to have no preconceived notions about strategy,
and to not rely on Elbereth (most bots rely on Elbereth and I wanted to
see what it would do instead). When it encountered the bigroom, this is
the strategy it adopted, and it worked quite well. (Specifically, it ran
round and round the edge of the map in circles until the monsters were
grouped following it, then picked them off in speed order.)

It was one of the most intelligent things I've ever seen it do
(especially because I was unaware of that strategy myself at the time).

